{"skill":{"slug":"telegram-api","displayName":"Telegram Bot"},"version":{"version":"1.2.9","createdAt":1790940495260,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":58270,"sha256":"40001b01fc080c6ad7d7f23e051cda652442ede215f15d8c92453ef0feed5590","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/calendly/triggers.md","size":10281,"sha256":"ae92dbfb6dd4caf628900b293d1b3c6e7d5e70cf7f6a9397407594daf50d4a48","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/github/triggers.md","size":61142,"sha256":"7424d3be38ec400eb8a4b0a6a94a94eeec40208c0bcee29a61caa5da48eea7f4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/google-mail/triggers.md","size":2648,"sha256":"5cc5065cd7db33dc33715675bbb0ee29ed49657ad9ad4354aebd1a9efdf8d8f3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/hubspot/triggers.md","size":8298,"sha256":"439d56e4d02e119e1de3caf79a0334243ae70c583a3e15847831c396f39c2837","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/linear/triggers.md","size":7270,"sha256":"641f6496f50e09faab921ef4c06f725122b798cb034e9f0dfaf9f838074ab377","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/notion/triggers.md","size":5840,"sha256":"fdaf3840d8213dbd7549426c1166f94cc94b09e022a1611ef2dad6f36db2f969","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/slack/triggers.md","size":6181,"sha256":"b5ee099a215223a7e5186c41a0d13fc1de68e977719304c509df105843d81f38","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/stripe/triggers.md","size":25651,"sha256":"ae091545396a376c7ecfe09e94b46b7bbb44fd8a72ea954bcc1239052b7959f0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/time/triggers.md","size":1140,"sha256":"b8f5a523501f8d03e11e58f6426cd96b54ba0c66c8983b57c0ea31386b309e01","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2324,"sha256":"a4bcc6298404a01cefd18c6542683ecb65d88c45ae3fdf72013f334f060220a9","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1790940802483,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3176f7c1a166b324d2d8d4cb5a53336a1ca691c2da3d058f3430d93f11d31407","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3176f7c1a166b324d2d8d4cb5a53336a1ca691c2da3d058f3430d93f11d31407","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1790940710692},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1790940802483},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed Telegram Bot API integration that uses Maton for authenticated API calls and documents the main risks around writes, credentials, webhooks, hosted functions, and persistent triggers.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill needs network access and managed authentication to call Telegram through Maton. Raw HTTP with a MATON_API_KEY is documented only as a fallback when the CLI cannot be installed, with warnings not to persist, print, or send the key elsewhere.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation uses pinned Maton CLI/package versions via npm or Homebrew and optional pinned SDK packages. This is proportionate for an API integration, but users should understand it installs a CLI and uses a Maton account.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions repeatedly require user approval for connection creation, writes, deletes, hosted functions, trigger destinations, webhooks, and local event execution; external API content is explicitly treated as untrusted data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Persistent elements include Maton login credentials in the OS credential store, Telegram connections, hosted functions, triggers, destinations, and Telegram webhooks. These are disclosed and paired with approval, scoping, and deletion guidance.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Telegram Bot API access through Maton, and the documented capabilities match that purpose: reading bot state, sending/editing/deleting messages, managing bot commands, webhooks, and optional automation via Maton functions and triggers.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to manage a Telegram bot through Maton. Pay special attention before approving message sends, deletes, setWebhook, trigger destinations, hosted functions, or raw API-key use, because those can create ongoing data flows or act on chats without further prompts if configured.","findings":"[SkillSpector] expected: SkillSpector reported no issues; artifact inspection found no contradictory hidden behavior.\n[AIG SARIF] expected: The static scan reported no results. High-impact features such as webhooks, trigger destinations, and local --exec are present in documentation but are explicitly scoped, user-approved, and purpose-aligned.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1790940802483}}}}}